cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Cite the original paper for the underlying scientific study. When using this
  notebook's figures, data or frozen-metric companion, also cite this dated
  work-in-progress record and specify the scientific snapshot and selected state.
type: software
title: A first experiment with AI agents in numerical geometry
version: 1.0.0
url: https://gbdl.github.io/4D-website/
repository-code: https://github.com/gbdl/4D-website
authors:
  - family-names: De Luca
    given-names: G. Bruno
    affiliation: LAPTh (CNRS and Université Savoie Mont Blanc), Annecy, France
abstract: >-
  An illustrated work-in-progress notebook about an initial attempt to use
  research agents on a four-dimensional numerical geometry problem. It compares
  the Local metric and Quotient metric, documents selected experiments and checks,
  and preserves unresolved Einstein-accuracy and compatibility limitations.
  The scientific evidence is frozen, with local accuracy and
  geometric compatibility remaining the joint numerical goal.
